Subject: [202505] Prepare pinned Python packages for cached wheel installation

A cold wheel build first installs dependencies into the builder user site.
Restoring a cached wheel skips that step, exposing Debian's distutils-owned
pexpect 4.8.0 to the later root pip install. The upstream 4.9.0 constraint
then fails because pip cannot uninstall that Debian package.

Install the pinned pexpect and pycparser copies into /usr/local before wheel
installation, without uninstalling or modifying Debian-owned files. Limit
--ignore-installed and --no-deps to these two packages; pexpect's ptyprocess
requirement is already supplied by Debian and pycparser has no dependencies.
All subsequent wheel installs retain normal dependency resolution and tests.
No upstream version constraints change.

Failure: https://github.com/ITJamie/sonic-vs-builder/actions/runs/42709123480
Tested against sonic-buildimage ff3c0c9f686a1d0dbddbe813b233b3b7a51bd8e2.
Remove when the builder handles Debian/pip ownership for cached wheel installs.

--- a/sonic-slave-bookworm/Dockerfile.j2
+++ b/sonic-slave-bookworm/Dockerfile.j2
@@ -554,6 +554,11 @@
 {%- endif %}
 {%- endif %}
 
+# Cached wheels skip the user-site dependency installation performed on a cold build.
+# Shadow these distutils packages without uninstalling Debian-owned files.
+# Versions match files/build/versions/build/build-sonic-slave-bookworm/versions-py3.
+RUN pip3 install --ignore-installed --no-deps pexpect==4.9.0 pycparser==3.0
+
 # For building sonic-utilities
 RUN pip3 install fastentrypoints mock
 
